PASS: single-tag legacy form works, multi-tag dispatch cuts every tag
on the same commit, the existing-tag refusal runs for every tag before
any tag is created, a failed atomic push leaves nothing on the
remote, and a mis-shaped policy tag (wrong case, stray slash or
whitespace) is refused at normalize time -- it can never reach
cut-release-gate.py's skip branch and get pushed ungated; and a degraded
publish's prerelease tag (ticket 43) normalizes cleanly and sorts BELOW
the clean number through the one shared parser; and the branch carrying
the signed evidence lands in the same atomic push as the tags, or not at
all (ticket 53).
